# UX workflow: verify bottom-left destructive action guardrails.
# Purpose: Step focus allows direct single-step reset, while step selection
# requires a long press before selected steps are reset.

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen track_focus

# Move from Track to Pattern to Step focus.
150 tap NAV 60
350 capture screen pattern_focus
450 tap NAV 60
650 capture screen step_focus

# Enable a visible step, then reset only that focused step with a tap.
750 tap MACRO_3 60
950 capture screen step_3_enabled
1050 tap BOTTOM_LEFT 60
1250 capture screen step_3_reset_by_tap

# Enable the same step again, enter step selection, and select it.
1350 tap MACRO_3 60
1550 capture screen step_3_reenabled
1650 button NAV down
2750 tick
2800 capture screen step_selection_entered
2850 button NAV up
3000 tap MACRO_3 60
3200 capture screen step_3_selected

# A short press must only cancel the armed state; the selected step remains.
3300 tap BOTTOM_LEFT 60
3500 capture screen selection_tap_does_not_reset

# Long press arms and applies the destructive selection reset.
3600 button BOTTOM_LEFT down
3800 capture screen selection_reset_hold_started
4700 tick
4750 capture screen selection_reset_applied_by_hold
4800 button BOTTOM_LEFT up
5050 capture screen selection_reset_released
